<Layout
  title="About | Mranmay Shetty"
  description="Mranmay Shetty’s path from electronics engineering to neuroscience."
>
  <div class="shell inner-page">
    <h1>About me</h1>
    <div class="about-body">
      <p class="lead">
        I came to neuroscience through engineering. I wanted to understand how a
        biological circuit does the things I was asking an artificial network to
        do.
      </p>
      <p>
        I studied electronics and telecommunication engineering at Symbiosis
        International University in Pune, then completed an MSc in Modeling for
        Neuronal and Cognitive Systems at Université Côte d’Azur.
      </p>
      <p>
        With Bruno Cessac at Inria, I explored how neural networks capture
        retinal dynamics. Working with Laurent Perrinet and Bruno on spike
        inference made me interested in what an imaging signal actually lets us
        say about a neuron.
      </p>
      <p>
        In Federico Rossi’s lab at IIT Rovereto, I studied how visual inputs are
        distributed across the dendrites of mouse cortical neurons. With Gabriel
        Kreiman, I’ve explored a complementary problem at the level of behavior
        and models. How do we keep track of an image across a sequence?
      </p>
      <p>
        Outside research, I enjoy gaming and previously competed in Call of Duty
        and PUBG.
      </p>
      <div class="page-links">
        <a class="button" href="/cv/">View CV</a><a
          class="text-link"
          href="/publications/">Publications</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
